! ax4b_156_test1_lvs.strap -- jb_ax4b "I-BOX 4", routine 1256 ("----I256---
! LVE AND LVS CHECK.", banner PDF p.173), its prologue and TEST 1, the
! LOAD VALUE WITH SUM test:
!
!   PDF p.173  012272.00-012274.40  I56: the prologue (SSIP's IDF1)
!   PDF p.173  012275.00            I56ID: location printed, NO code
!   PDF p.173  012276.00-012313.40  I561: TEST 1A, IX 0-2
!   PDF p.174  012314.00-012333.40  TEST 1A, IX 3-10
!   PDF p.175  012334.00-012351.40  TEST 1A, IX 11-15, exit, continuity
!   PDF p.176  012352.00-012375.40  I562: TEST 1B, IX 00-01
!   PDF pp.177-181  012376.00-012531.40  TEST 1B, IX 02-15, the zero-mask
!                                   check, exit, continuity
!   PDF p.189  012774.00            IC256, "-CONTINUITY REG 1256."
!   PDF p.190  012776.00, 013035.00 156K1 (CNOP before it prints nothing),
!                                   1000 ("INDX WD. OF ONES.")
!   PDF p.191  013054.00-013073.00  BIT0-BIT15
!
! No printed page numbers on these sheets: cited by PDF page and octal
! location.  Read from the page images at 150 dpi; checked row for row
! against the printed machine code by
! tests/verify_ax4b_156_test1_lvs_listing.py.
!
! THE BANNER, verbatim (p.173):
!         -THIS TEST IS COMPOSED OF TWO MAJOR ROUTINES
!         -WHICH TEST THE ABOVE AS FOLLOWS,
!                 -TEST 1 CHECKS THAT LVS WILL
!                     -LOAD CORRECTLY FROM EACH IX,
!                     -AND THAT EACH IX REG CAN BE
!                     -LOADED WITH THE SOME OF ALL
!                     -THE OTHERS.
!                 -TEST 2 CHECKS THAT LVE WILL LOAD
!                     -CORRECTLY WITH 5 LEVELS, AND
!                     -UNDER ALL CONDITIONS.
! ("SOME" is IBM's spelling.)  TEST 2 is decks/ax4b_156_test2_lve.strap.
!
! WHY IT MATTERS.  Until now LVS rested on the Reference Manual alone
! (printed p.28, PDF 31; decks/lvs_multiple_indexing.strap).  This is
! IBM's own test of it:
!   TEST 1A  Xk = BITk's index word (value bit k), k = 0..15.
!            LVS,$X15,$X0 then LVS,$X0,$Xk for k = 1..15: a one-bit
!            mask copies exactly Xk's value ("LVS ADDRESSING OF IX k
!            FAILS.").  The masks print 400000.37 0B ... 4.01 0B.
!   TEST 1B  for every k: LVS,$Xk,$0,...,$15 (mask 777774, all sixteen)
!            must give bits 0-15 = 156K1 (777774.00), the sum of BIT0-
!            BIT15 -- including Xk's own old value; then
!            LX,$Xk,$Xk (index storage, address 16+k) and BZXCZ: the
!            count must still be zero ("LVS DESTROYS COUNT FIELD.");
!            SR,$Xk,$Xk, LX,$Xk,$Xk and BZXVZ: the refill field, stored
!            into the value field, must be zero ("LVS DESTROYS REFILL
!            FIELD."); LX,$Xk,BITk restores Xk.
!            Last, SVA,$X6,$+.32 zeroes the mask of the NEXT half-word,
!            "$LVS,$X1,0" (assembled as LVS,$X1,$0: "400000.03 0B"),
!            and the store-modified LVS must clear X1's value from all
!            ones (1000) -- "ZEROS IN 0-15 OF LVS FAILS TO CLEAR
!            SPECIFIED IX REG."  A store into the very next half-word,
!            which the look-ahead may already hold.
!
! TWO SEGMENTS.  TEST 1A ends in its own "B,SSW" (TO SSIP) at
! 012347.40 and TEST 1B at 012527.40.  With SSW a PASS halt the driver
! runs this deck twice: from END (I56, the prologue, which falls into
! I561 through SSIP's IDF1) and with ENTRY=I562.  The continuity rows
! after each B,SSW are transcribed and verified but never run.
!
! RESULT, 2026-11-19: both segments PASS IBM's checks (PC 1410, SEN 0).
!   I56 (END: prologue, TEST 1A): RET's word (001306) = 0x52f0800, the
!     return to 012274.00 (half-word 24570 octal); X0 = X15 =
!     0x1000000000000; CYCLES 1209.
!   I562 (TEST 1B): X0 = X1 = 0x7fffffffff -- the value field zeroed by
!     the zero-mask check, count and refill all ones kept from I000;
!     X15 = 0x1000000000000; CYCLES 2927.
!   CYCLES is MODEL BEHAVIOUR.
! MODEL INJECTIONS, OBSERVED (each in its own scratch copy of bsv/, all
! eight routine-1256 runs and the I48 run repeated):
!   B1 LVS reads the mask in reverse (ii.imm[3 + n] for ii.imm[18 - n])
!     -> I56 FAIL: SEN 0x531e00000000000 (a TEST 1A SIC,SEN), X0
!     0x8000000000000000, X15 0, PC 1416 (SERS), CYCLES 483.  I562
!     PASSES: TEST 1B's masks are all sixteen registers, symmetric under
!     the reversal, and its zero-mask check survives too; so I562 does
!     not discriminate bit order.  No TEST 2 run moves.
!   B2 LVS writes the sum into the COUNT field too -> I56 FAIL (X0
!     0x1000004000000, its count no longer 0); I562 FAIL: SEN
!     0x53d600000000000, X0 0xffff000ffc000000, X1 0x4000000000000000,
!     PC 1416, CYCLES 429.  No TEST 2 run moves.
!   The LVE injections (C1-C3, D1, D2; see ax4b_156_test2_lve.strap)
!     leave both runs passing.
!   CONTROL: the unmodified model in the same scratch arrangement: all
!     nine runs PASS with the pins in run_tests.sh.
!
! SUBSTITUTIONS (not on these pages):
!   * SSIP's entry points at the addresses PDF p.193's SYN table prints
!     (SSW 1301.0, SERS 1304.0, RET 1306.40, SEN 1310.0, SENO 1311.0,
!     DPET13 1437.0, IDF1 1443.0).  SSW is a PASS halt, SERS a FAIL
!     halt, SEN/SENO data words SIC stores into.  RET is a "$B,0"
!     half-word whose address field SIC,RET fills and IDF1 ("print ID")
!     is a bare branch to it: that return path is INFERRED from routine
!     148's own idiom (SIC,148S2 / B,148S1 returning through 148S2's
!     "$B,0", PDF pp.114, 152); no SSIP page shows IDF1's body.  DPET13
!     is a data word.  SIC "is executed if and only if the associated
!     branching is successful" (Reference Manual printed p.41, PDF 44),
!     so SEN stays 0 on a pass and names the error entry on a failure.
!   * Notation only: "%" and the box glyph are "(" and ")"; the label
!     glyph the scan shows as "1" is the letter I (I56.., I000), as for
!     every ax4b label (docs/listing_typography.md).  The register list
!     "$0,$1,...,$15" is IBM's own spelling and is kept.
!   * I56ID prints a location and no code, so it is SYN'd; the word
!     there is not in this image.
!
! ---- SSIP's entry points: SUBSTITUTES (not on these pages) -----------
        SLC, (8)1301.0
SSW     BEW, $                        ! SUBSTITUTE: PASS (the return to SSIP)
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERS    BEW, $                        ! SUBSTITUTE: FAIL (SSIP's error report)
        SLC, (8)1306.40
RET     $B, 0                         ! SUBSTITUTE: SSIP's return half-word
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SEN     DD(BU,64,8), 0                ! SUBSTITUTE: SIC's error link word
SENO    DD(BU,64,8), 0                ! SUBSTITUTE: SIC's other link word
        SLC, (8)1437.0
DPET13  DD(BU,64), 0                  ! SUBSTITUTE: SSIP's ident cell
        SLC, (8)1443.0
IDF1    B, RET                        ! SUBSTITUTE: SSIP's "print ID"
!
! ======================================================================
! PDF p.173, 012272.00-012274.40: routine 1256's prologue
! ======================================================================
        SLC, (8)12272.0
I56     LX, $X1, I56ID                ! -UPDATE IDENT.
        SX, $X1, DPET13
        SIC, RET
        B, IDF1                       ! -PRINT ID.
        Z, IC256
        BD, I561
        CNOP
! I56ID  %IQSZ@DD%BU,64,8@,I256     Z        012275.00, no machine code
I56ID   SYN, (8)12275.0
!
